1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 {Surely Black can no longer try c5 here—or can Black?} 3.
Nf3 Nf6 4. e3 e6 (4... Bf5 5. Nc3 e6 {This really is an exception in which Black manages without e5 or c5, but the pieces have been developed well.}) 5. b3 (5. Nc3 {Transposition to the Meran!}) 5... Bd6 6. Bb2 O-O $1
7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. O-O $1 Qe7 9. Qc2 e5 {Black adopts the central setup.} *

