1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bb4 $5 {A very modern system in which Black must be prepared to play either c5 or e5.} 5. Qa4+ (5. e3
{is actually a transposition to the Nimzo-Indian} O-O 6. Bd3 c5 {This is the queenside setup, but with ...Bb4.}) 5... Nc6 {Black can no longer play c5 here. Within the queenside system this would be a complete dead end, but...} 6. e3 O-O 7.
Bd2 dxc4 8. Bxc4 Bd7 9. Qc2 Bd6 10. O-O e5 {[%csl Yd5,Ye5] Black adopts the central setup!} *

