[White "Queenside Setup"]
[Black "Carlsbad Example"]
[Result "*"]
[ECO "D36"]
[Annotator "ChessTutor"]
[PlyCount "20"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 (5. e3 $6 c6 6. Bd3 Bd6 7. b3
O-O 8. Bb2 Re8 {Fundamentally, the Nimzo-Indian setup is a queenside setup in which Black retains flexibility by delaying ...d5. This may allow Black to avoid unfavourable pawn structures. The underlying objective, however, remains exactly the same!}) 5... c6 6. e3 Be7 7. Bd3 O-O 8. Qc2 Nbd7 9. Nf3 (9.
Nge2 $5 Re8 10. O-O Nf8 11. f3 {Grandmasters play this here and claim that, in ...d5 structures, the early Nf3 gives them easier play.}) 9... Re8 10. O-O Nf8 {Queen's Indian} *

