1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 (3. Nf3 Bg7 {[%cal Gh7h5,Gh5h4,Yf8h7,Yh7g5,Rb3b4,Rb4b5,Ra2a4] A King's Indian Attack for Black: the kingside setup. There is no ...f5, but Black attacks White. The general question is who will be faster on their respective wing.} 4. e3 O-O 5. b3 d6 6. Bb2 Re8 7.
Be2 {is called the Grünfeld. Black fights for the centre without ...e6.} Nbd7 (7... Nc6 8. O-O e5 9. Nc3 exd4 10. exd4 d5 $11
{[%csl Gc5,Gd5] This is still the queenside setup, only without ...e6.}) 8. O-O e5 9. Nc3 e4 10. Nd2 Nf8 $13 {White has a mixture of the central and queenside setups. Guess what Black is aiming for...}) 3... Bg7 (3... d5 {[%csl Gc7,Gd6,Ge5,Gg6,Gh7][%cal Yf7f5] the kingside setup!} 4. Bf4 Bg7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3
c5 {There are also sideline systems, but the basic setup must be understood there as well.}) 4.
e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4] White's central setup} e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 {A useful tip: simply exchange the bishops.} *

